{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions","id":3533,"title":"Scion General Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T08:52:02-08:00","id":3533,"title":"Scion General Questions","content":"I figure a topic to put all sorts of general questions would be nice, and as someone mostly new to Scion, I figure it'll help me out too. <hr /><br /> <br /> Can Scions of Vodoun be other ethnicities than African?<br /> Can Scions of Amatsukami be other ethnicities than Japanese?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T11:38:48-08:00","id":3644,"title":"","content":"There's nothing stopping them - the other core four are willing to look outside their originating cultures, after all (and April Fool's Day's <i>Scion: Extras</i> has a redneck Loa Scion and a South Korean Amatsukami Scion). There's a thing with Scion NPCs being tied to their pantheon's originating culture - my fanon theory would be some pantheons prefer Scions who're linked to the culture, but they're willing to look outside if someone catches their eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 11-05-2013, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:36:17-08:00","id":3687,"title":"","content":"It would stand out a little for some pantheons, but not that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:56:50-08:00","id":3702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions#post3533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Scions of Vodoun be other ethnicities than African?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Especially if we go with the pantheon of Vodoun and not the original African religions. New Orleans alone has thousands of people from many differing ethnic backgrounds who follow the beliefs of Vodoun. Scion has no rules against the culture or heritage of a character. It would be a little easier to explain background-wise, but if you've got a good reason as to say ... a girl from Alaska is Visited as a child of the Baron in New Orleans, go for it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions#post3533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Scions of Amatsukami be other ethnicities than Japanese?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same answer as above, but with a twist. The Japanese are very xenophobic. One can only assume this view on outside cultures and races mirrored in their gods. While I see no problem in a scion being sired on, say, an American military wife in Okinawa; that child would be considered at best a half-breed in the gods' eyes and might face a lot of hardships being recognized and gaining status within the pantheon itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:10:48-08:00","id":3750,"title":"","content":"Most pantheons are at least somewhat xenophobic, so it's far more likely that the Scions in question are going to be similar in ethnicity to the peoples who worshipped them. That being said, as Aynie points out, there's no reason a Scion of a pantheon CAN'T be of a different ethnicity, but doing so is going to probably cause some issues, or at least weird looks. It depends on the pantheon in general, and also individual gods. The Aztecs were pretty racist, but Quetzalcoatl, being a god worshipped from Arizona to Nicaragua, is likely to be less concerned about a Scion being some other race.<br /> <br /> Also to note is that with enough Appearance Knacks, the Scion can be any ethnicity they want. And Human Clay has the potential craziness of asking a Health God to actually change their ethnicity<br /> <br /> I kind of want to have a game where every member of the Band is a different ethnicity than their pantheon. Chinese Loa. Mexican Kami. Samoan Aesir. Tons of possibilities here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:51:34-08:00","id":3777,"title":"","content":"Wowzas, then what sort of Pantheon would people from the Great Plains of the USA be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:02:28-08:00","id":3785,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Demigod had a mixed race Scion of Tyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/791-chrysander","name":"Chrysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:13:41-08:00","id":3788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=3777#post3777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wowzas, then what sort of Pantheon would people from the Great Plains of the USA be?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of Scandinavians here, so Norse. Maybe some Greek and the Occasional Loa or Azlanti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T02:34:10-08:00","id":4169,"title":"","content":"Also, remember that the iconic Egyptian and his counterpart are american and to all appearances caucasian. The counterpart to the iconic Loa was mixed blood herself. Additionally in the companion book they make specific reference to a caucasian or at the very least non Japanese scion of Amateratsu. <br /> <br /> A thought that occurs to me is that by the time they are gods they are wholly beings of ichor. They're pantheon is their ethnicity despite what form their god bodies take especially considering how bestial those bodies can be in appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:03:32-08:00","id":4383,"title":"","content":"There are rules for gods adopting. IIRC at least one deity (Diana?) only adopts. Any deity can have any ethnicity as a Scion child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T14:58:41-08:00","id":5442,"title":"","content":"They do mention in a few points gods adopting. Diana, as well as in the Celestial Beauracracy in Companion. As for American Scions, bear in mind America is a melting pot of every culture and race. Pretty much every pantheon would be easy to represent in an American citizen. Though if you want to go Cliche, there IS a &quot;Yankee&quot; pantheon in the Companion with people like Paul Bunyan, Pecos Bill, John Henry, Johnny Appleseed.<br /> <br /> Aside from particular racial issues (Like Japanese insane level of xenophobia, and that leading to a relatively unlikely white Amatsukami Scion) nothing is stopping you from doing what you want. A) They're gods. They do what they please. B) It's a game, so who really cares. I once made Charles Bronson (Convict, not actor. See the Tom Hardy film Bronson) as a Scion of Sun Wukong on account of England's hold of Hong Kong for a long period of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:35:02-08:00","id":5605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=4169#post4169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought that occurs to me is that by the time they are gods they are wholly beings of ichor. They're pantheon is their ethnicity despite what form their god bodies take especially considering how bestial those bodies can be in appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Also, good point referring to the nonhuman appearances not afflicting the Scion with a nonhuman appearance. Wasn't Zeus in the form of a swan when he sired Perseus? Or am I confusing that with the mediocre new Clash of the Titans movie?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T20:53:31-08:00","id":5715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=5605#post5605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this. Also, good point referring to the nonhuman appearances not afflicting the Scion with a nonhuman appearance. Wasn't Zeus in the form of a swan when he sired Perseus? Or am I confusing that with the mediocre new Clash of the Titans movie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Perseus is the result of Zeus raining down on his mother as a shower of gold while she's locked up. The swan was with Leda and produced the twins Castor and Pollux and Helen and her twin (I can never remember that one!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T02:48:42-08:00","id":5783,"title":"","content":"Ethnicity is never a concern mechanically speaking, it is only a concern for roleplaying reasons. Some gods may be 'enlightened' with modern first world values, but you can always expect some gods to cling to their bronze age mentality with the passion of a thousand burning stars. That means racism, elitism, nepotism, cronyism, jingoism and a bunch of other 'isms that have the potential to spice up your game and make life a roller coaster for your players.<br /> <br /> <b>But part of the fun of choosing an outlier is overcoming or embracing those negative expectations.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T06:10:24-08:00","id":5853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions#post3533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Scions of Vodoun be other ethnicities than African?<br /> Can Scions of Amatsukami be other ethnicities than Japanese?</div> </div> </div> </div>From looking at the real world I would think it would depend not just on the culture, but the deity him/herself.<br /> I think a lot of people like to delude themselves in thinking that there is an inherent superiority in their culture...or in the other direction, they think that they are more accepting. That's always something that can be played out. Especially if there's a different religion for the scion to begin with. I think most deities with a lot of chaos in them would be the ones that snatch such scions up. For example, I think the only deity in the Norse pantheon that would accept a &quot;gypsy&quot; would be Loki.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T07:09:46-08:00","id":5881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=5853#post5853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From looking at the real world I would think it would depend not just on the culture, but the deity him/herself.<br /> I think a lot of people like to delude themselves in thinking that there is an inherent superiority in their culture...or in the other direction, they think that they are more accepting. That's always something that can be played out. Especially if there's a different religion for the scion to begin with. I think most deities with a lot of chaos in them would be the ones that snatch such scions up. For example, I think the only deity in the Norse pantheon that would accept a &quot;gypsy&quot; would be Loki.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Ragnarok book specifically states that the Aesir are very accepting of miscegenation. They already are the result of intermarriage between two separate pantheons and the giants, who are technically Titanspawn. They really don't have a problem with taking lovers from other ethnicities or even other species.<br /> <br /> Thor sired two sons on a giantess. Freyr is MARRIED to one. So's Uller. If the Aesir don't mind three of their most potent members being with members of a race who are technically their enemies, then having sex with a human of African or Asian extraction is nothing to them.<br /> <br /> Also, as has already been pointed out, Demigod introduces a Scion of Tyr whose mother was black. Nothing unusual about him. He just looks like a typical example of a mating between a black woman and a white man. Now, we didn't get a lot of information about him or his relationship with the other Aesir, but there's nothing to suggest that he's treated any differently.<br /> <br /> With their Loyalty virtue, the Aesir care a lot more about whether or not you're doing your part to help the family than they do about what your parentage is. If you're pulling your weight, that's all that matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T08:53:41-08:00","id":5982,"title":"","content":"The Norse weren't just accepting of it, they encouraged it, for the boys at least. Guys were encouraged to marry women outside the clan, so to speak, to bring new blood in. Women, on the other hand, were discouraged from doing so because the clan didn't want to lose them to another. It was a part of Scandinavian culture that you can definitely see reflected in their myths. In fact, it's very interesting to note that Loki's case is the only instance we really know of where a female god has a kid whose father is a frost giant. Meaning that Loki, so unlike the rest of the Aesir anyway, had something of a stigma attached to him from birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/545-lesingnon","name":"Lesingnon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar545_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T09:07:33-08:00","id":5995,"title":"","content":"I think it is worth noting that the ethnicities we associate with the specific religions the Pantheons are based on are largely historical over-simplifications. The wide-spread culture of maintaining ethnic &quot;purity&quot; by selective breeding is far more modern than most people consider. The Pantheons essentially predate it. Some of them would have members that care about breeding for personal reasons, and some of them are going to be influenced more by the relative isolation of the religions that spawned them, but in the end it is doubtful that &quot;what you look like&quot; is important to most of them beyond their own personal standards of what looks worth making a divine baby with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T09:10:22-08:00","id":6000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lesingnon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=5982#post5982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Norse weren't just accepting of it, they encouraged it, for the boys at least. Guys were encouraged to marry women outside the clan, so to speak, to bring new blood in. Women, on the other hand, were discouraged from doing so because the clan didn't want to lose them to another. It was a part of Scandinavian culture that you can definitely see reflected in their myths. In fact, it's very interesting to note that Loki's case is the only instance we really know of where a female god has a kid whose father is a frost giant. Meaning that Loki, so unlike the rest of the Aesir anyway, had something of a stigma attached to him from birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Loki was the child of two giants? Farbauti and Laufey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T09:38:00-08:00","id":6064,"title":"","content":"Well if a group wants to add the idea to their game then I would still look at the real world for examples of racism, which despite it's existence tends to be swept under the rug.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T13:53:06-08:00","id":7018,"title":"","content":"I have a new question about Birthrights.<br /> <br /> So, the way I understand it, a Scion can initially only use Purviews that s/he shares with his/her parent and their Birthright can only grant them the ability to use those. Though, in the character example &quot;Donnie Rhodes' &quot; birthright was the Daedelus Device, which gives him purviews not associated with Aphrodite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:39:15-08:00","id":7039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=7018#post7018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a new question about Birthrights.<br /> <br /> So, the way I understand it, a Scion can initially only use Purviews that s/he shares with his/her parent and their Birthright can only grant them the ability to use those. Though, in the character example &quot;Donnie Rhodes' &quot; birthright was the Daedelus Device, which gives him purviews not associated with Aphrodite.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they can use any of their boons so long as they have their relic except for their pantheon specific purview. Once they hot demigod they can use boons associated with their parent without their relic at legend -1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:40:30-08:00","id":7040,"title":"","content":"<b>Heroes</b> can use any All Purpose Purview or Special Purview they desire, provided they have have a Relic that channels that purview. Naturally, you also have to buy the Boon you desire to activate within any given purview.<br /> <br /> Of course, you have to explain how you got a Relic that channels a purview your parent does not normally have access to. The parent could channel that purview themselves (just not at Avatar level), or call in a favor from a friend, or have a bunch of trophies lying around, or some other god or legendary creature could have given it to your Hero for their own countless inscrutable reasons. It can be as big a plot hook, or as small a plot hook as you want to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:53:40-08:00","id":7048,"title":"","content":"Scions don't need to share the Purview with their Divine Parent, all they need is a Relic to access the Purview. RAW, these Relics can only be created by a God with the same Purview as the Relic will give. This means that your Divine Parent will have to trade favors for some Relics that are outside their area of influence. (Unless they are a Deity who creates things, like Hephaestus, who should be able to make whatever he wants)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:54:05-08:00","id":17290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=7048#post7048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions don't need to share the Purview with their Divine Parent, all they need is a Relic to access the Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=7040#post7040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Heroes</b> can use any All Purpose Purview or Special Purview they desire, provided they have have a Relic that channels that purview. Naturally, you also have to buy the Boon you desire to activate within any given purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything preventing a Scion from buying a Boon for which he does not have a Relic giving him access to that Purview? For example, if his Relic was stolen, or if he hopes to be gifted (or plans on stealing or otherwise acquiring) such a Relic? Or... can only the owner of a relic purchase new Boons from that Purview?<br /> <br /> For example, supposing Scion 1 had a Relic which granted access to the Sky Purview. Scion 1 then took the &quot;Wind's Freedom&quot; Boon, allowing him to fly. Scion 2 then steals this Relic. The Hero book says, &quot;If the item is stolen, however, not only does the Scion lose access to the Boons, but the thief gains access to them for as long as he possesses the stolen Birthright.&quot; So, Scion 2 now has access to Sky and to the &quot;Wind's Freedom&quot; Boon? Which of the 2 Scions (or both or neither) can spend XP to purchase the Sky Boon &quot;Sky's Grace&quot; while the Relic is still stolen?<br /> <br /> And... although I can't find it in the rules, I seem to recall someone telling me that, if Scion 1 in the above example dies, a) Scion 2 loses access to &quot;Wind's Freedom&quot; (but the Relic still continues to grant access to the Sky Purview); b) Scion 2 can now claim the wings as &quot;his&quot;, no longer suffering penalties for using someone else's relic. Is that true?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=7048#post7048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, these Relics can only be created by a God with the same Purview as the Relic will give. This means that your Divine Parent will have to trade favors for some Relics that are outside their area of influence.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=7040#post7040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, you have to explain how you got a Relic that channels a purview your parent does not normally have access to. The parent could channel that purview themselves (just not at Avatar level), or call in a favor from a friend, or have a bunch of trophies lying around, or some other god or legendary creature could have given it to your Hero for their own countless inscrutable reasons. It can be as big a plot hook, or as small a plot hook as you want to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if the Scion, or their divine parent, acquires relics from other deities (or even other pantheons?), there is no inherent fatebinding or anything like that? Are the quantity of Birthright Relics in storage as left up to the individual story as the size of the plot hook surrounding their acquisition is?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:27:31-08:00","id":17309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17290#post17290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything preventing a Scion from buying a Boon for which he does not have a Relic giving him access to that Purview? For example, if his Relic was stolen, or if he hopes to be gifted (or plans on stealing or otherwise acquiring) such a Relic? Or... can only the owner of a relic purchase new Boons from that Purview?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You can buy whatever Boons you have the Legend to justify, but you won't be able to <i>use</i> that Boon without an appropriate Relic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17290#post17290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, supposing Scion 1 had a Relic which granted access to the Sky Purview. Scion 1 then took the &quot;Wind's Freedom&quot; Boon, allowing him to fly. Scion 2 then steals this Relic. The Hero book says, &quot;If the item is stolen, however, not only does the Scion lose access to the Boons, but the thief gains access to them for as long as he possesses the stolen Birthright.&quot; So, Scion 2 now has access to Sky and to the &quot;Wind's Freedom&quot; Boon? Which of the 2 Scions (or both or neither) can spend XP to purchase the Sky Boon &quot;Sky's Grace&quot; while the Relic is still stolen?</div> </div> </div> </div>This.. is a really weird part of the system. Basically, Scion 1 spent the XP and still has <b>Wind's Freedom </b>on his character sheet. He just can't <i>use</i> it without a Relic. Maybe he has two Relics that channel Sky, or steals a Sky Relic from someone else. He can still use <b>Wind's Freedom </b>just fine. But, for as long as Scion 2 has the stolen Relic, they can <i>also</i> use <b>Wind's Freedom</b>, along with any other Sky Boons known to Scion 1. Basically he's &quot;borrowing&quot; Scion 1's Boons for as long as he has that stolen Relic.<br /> <br /> As I said, that's a <i>really</i> weird part of the system and it strongly encourages &quot;cheating&quot; by passing around your Relics to your friends so they can use your Boons and you can use theirs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17290#post17290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... although I can't find it in the rules, I seem to recall someone telling me that, if Scion 1 in the above example dies, a) Scion 2 loses access to &quot;Wind's Freedom&quot; (but the Relic still continues to grant access to the Sky Purview); b) Scion 2 can now claim the wings as &quot;his&quot;, no longer suffering penalties for using someone else's relic. Is that true?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. None of this is true. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17290#post17290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if the Scion, or their divine parent, acquires relics from other deities (or even other pantheons?), there is no inherent fatebinding or anything like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You can be a starting Scion from the Aesir, but say that one of your Relics was given to you by Ares because you did him a favor one time. There's no penalty or anything. Your Relics can come from anywhere at all. Your starting Relics, and Demigod or God Relics, are assumed to be Bound to you, no matter who actually gave them to you. So if Ares gives our example Norse Scion a sword that channels War, it's exactly the same as if Odin had given it to the Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17290#post17290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the quantity of Birthright Relics in storage as left up to the individual story as the size of the plot hook surrounding their acquisition is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean by &quot;Relics in storage&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T16:24:12-08:00","id":17369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17309#post17309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This.. is a really weird part of the system. Basically, Scion 1 spent the XP and still has <b>Wind's Freedom </b>on his character sheet. He just can't <i>use</i> it without a Relic. Maybe he has two Relics that channel Sky, or steals a Sky Relic from someone else. He can still use <b>Wind's Freedom </b>just fine. But, for as long as Scion 2 has the stolen Relic, they can <i>also</i> use <b>Wind's Freedom</b>, along with any other Sky Boons known to Scion 1. Basically he's &quot;borrowing&quot; Scion 1's Boons for as long as he has that stolen Relic.<br /> <br /> As I said, that's a <i>really</i> weird part of the system and it strongly encourages &quot;cheating&quot; by passing around your Relics to your friends so they can use your Boons and you can use theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my head - I could take 5 1-dot relics to grant access to the Sky Purview, take all the Sky Boons, and gave one relic to each of my friends. That's crazy hacks. Um... wait... why don't the gods just give their Scions Relics which are attuned, instead of to the Scion, but to the deity him- or her-self? Sure, it's harder to use, but... free boons. Is there any reason this would be a bad plan?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17309#post17309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what you mean by &quot;Relics in storage&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, this was probably the least interesting part of the post - I was just asking, if, to access a Purview he usually doesn't have, a deity can give his/her Scion a stolen/traded relic that was being kept in storage, whether the number of such relics he has in storage is completely arbitrary, and left up to the individual story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T16:29:30-08:00","id":17373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17369#post17369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my head - I could take 5 1-dot relics to grant access to the Sky Purview, take all the Sky Boons, and gave one relic to each of my friends. That's crazy hacks. Um... wait... why don't the gods just give their Scions Relics which are attuned, instead of to the Scion, but to the deity him- or her-self? Sure, it's harder to use, but... free boons. Is there any reason this would be a bad plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is <i>exactly</i> why that system is so. damn. stupid. Everything you just said is 100% possible and effective. It's super, SUPER lame. I think most folks just ignore the &quot;stolen Relic&quot; rules. Stealing a Relic just gets you a Relic. Not access to someone else's Boons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17369#post17369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, this was probably the least interesting part of the post - I was just asking, if, to access a Purview he usually doesn't have, a deity can give his/her Scion a stolen/traded relic that was being kept in storage, whether the number of such relics he has in storage is completely arbitrary, and left up to the individual story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. That can be and is done. It doesn't have to come from 'storage', but could be a favor traded with another God or something. If Freyr wants to give his son a Death Relic, he could trade a favor to Odin or Hel for it. Or, maybe he wants to give his son an Animal Relic but no Aesir have Animal, so he could trade a favor with one of the Irish who do have Animal, like the Morrigan. Basically you can take a Relic for anything you want, and you have <i>immense</i> freedom to figure out how your parent got it for you. It lets you set up a ton of cool situations where your PC is already connected to other Gods or Pantheons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T17:52:08-08:00","id":17403,"title":"","content":"I've got a small general question: which direction should Rivalries be read? For example, in the Hero book, for Rivals, Artemis lists Susano-o. Susano-o, on the other hand, does not list Artemis as a Rival. My play group is split on whether that means Artemis picks on (scions of) Susano-o, or whether that means that Susano-o picks on scions of Artemis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T18:01:07-08:00","id":17410,"title":"","content":"Rivalries are kinda crap. I'd just ignore them. The idea is that they represent other figures that specific God doesn't get along with, but since there is no &quot;default setting&quot; for the game, it doesn't really make sense to have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T15:57:09-08:00","id":18780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=17373#post17373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is <i>exactly</i> why that system is so. damn. stupid. Everything you just said is 100% possible and effective. It's super, SUPER lame. I think most folks just ignore the &quot;stolen Relic&quot; rules. Stealing a Relic just gets you a Relic. Not access to someone else's Boons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Woody, we can assume that this &quot;house rule&quot; of ignoring the free boons is in effect in our game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T19:03:47-08:00","id":20463,"title":"","content":"Does Scion have a &quot;Masquerade&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T20:07:01-08:00","id":20478,"title":"","content":"Nope. Not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T20:29:54-08:00","id":20483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=20478#post20478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's what I thought. My friend asked and I said no, and he wondered if that meant there was constant media coverage on the activities of the Godborn or whatever. I figured there was cause of the Heku power that gives them legend when people talk about them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T20:57:26-08:00","id":20489,"title":"","content":"That's up to the Storyteller. There might be 24-hour Scion News Coverage, or maybe there's a worldwide government conspiracy to try covering it all up to prevent panic and revolution. It depends on what kind of game you want, and what level of power. At Hero, mortals can probably suppress the news. By Demigod? No way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T21:17:05-08:00","id":20495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=20483#post20483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, that's what I thought. My friend asked and I said no, and he wondered if that meant there was constant media coverage on the activities of the Godborn or whatever. I figured there was cause of the Heku power that gives them legend when people talk about them</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to change in the settings of Scion 2e.<br /> <br /> As of first edition, it's heavily implied that your band's exploits are becoming world-famous. Legendary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T19:49:37-08:00","id":20946,"title":"","content":"So for someone who hasn't got any of the books, but is interested in the game mechanics, is it possible to have a Scion who's parent was a titan?<br /> <br /> <br /> I ask, because I was thinking of making a Cthulhu Scion, but according to the website I looked up, The Great Old Ones are classified as Titans (yet calls them gods, oddly enough).<br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking it might be possible if a Titan Spawn / Scion decided to switch sides and work for the other team if they might be considered one or the other. I've already read a couple notes around here saying how some gods choose to 'adopt' scions, rather than actually sire them, and wondered if that could apply to children of the opposing factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T00:47:02-08:00","id":21038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=20946#post20946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for someone who hasn't got any of the books, but is interested in the game mechanics, is it possible to have a Scion who's parent was a titan?<br /> I ask, because I was thinking of making a Cthulhu Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The official answer is:</b> No, and No.<br /> <br /> <b>The first unofficial answer is:</b> Sometimes a titan might have had a Scion before he or she became a titan. Or your storyteller wants to handwave the issue and say that titans are entirely capable of having Scions on their own (especially if the storyteller wants to call into question what it means to be a titanspawn).<br /> <br /> <b>The second unofficial answer is:</b> Cthulhu is not a mythological figure and ineligible for any of the above advice. Or your storyteller wants to handwave the issue and say that fictional entities are entirely capable of having Scions in this particular game. I don't recommend it, but it is not my game. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:03:11-08:00","id":21369,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by fictional entity? I would think that would apply to all Titans / Pantheons<br /> <br /> &gt;:3<br /> <br /> Anyways, the site I got the information off had a list of a lot of Pantheons both fan made and official. They were based on various gods or god-like entities throughout history including the Saints (of Catholicism), The Great Old Ones (of Lovecraft), The Storied (of fairy tales and folk legends), The Ghedan (neanderthal gods) the Ani-Matsu (anime conversion), and even the very Chaos Gods (Warhammer 40k conversion)!<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason why I wanted to know if there was a difference, was because The Great Old Ones on the wiki are classified as Gods (i.e God of Chaos, God of Gateways, God of Fertility, est) but their description calls them Titans. So I wasn't sure if Gods and Titans were the same race but different factions, and thus both able to produce Scions or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-01-2013, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:16:54-08:00","id":21374,"title":"","content":"I think that considering how utterly alien Lovecraft's Gods are, that would make one strange game to run from a scion perspective. Aren't the &quot;deep ones&quot; created from humans? I don't want to think of what children there might be. The gods were supposed to be alien in every way including as to how they think.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, and more to the point <i>imagine</i>, the game would be pretty horrific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T22:15:25-08:00","id":21451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=21369#post21369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by fictional entity? I would think that would apply to all Titans / Pantheons</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and insisting otherwise may start a huge flame war. I would recommend against it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:56:14-08:00","id":21668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=20495#post20495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's going to change in the settings of Scion 2e.<br /> <br /> As of first edition, it's heavily implied that your band's exploits are becoming world-famous. Legendary!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo there will be a setting for Scion 2e?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=21369#post21369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by fictional entity? I would think that would apply to all Titans / Pantheons</div> </div> </div> </div>As a polytheist, I will strongly disagree with this statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:28:16-08:00","id":21696,"title":"","content":"I've always thought better of most of the Titans that the Greek Gods have fought against.<br /> <br /> I've often been curious of how truly &quot;evil&quot; were the old gods that the newer gods had to fight against (and possibly demonize) to justify their own position.<br /> <br /> Medusa's fate was so unjust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:52:18-08:00","id":21721,"title":"","content":"In most cases, the new Gods are the heroes simply because they're the winners. There are few things, after all, that Kronos has done that Zeus has not.<br /> <br /> It's a moot point as far as Scion is concerned though. It doesn't really matter how good or evil individual Titan Avatars are. What matters is that the Greater Titans have no purpose but to flood existence with their elements. You may think Odin is a total manipulative jerk, but better him than letting the whole world burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:54:49-08:00","id":21724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=21696#post21696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought better of most of the Titans that the Greek Gods have fought against.<br /> <br /> I've often been curious of how truly &quot;evil&quot; were the old gods that the newer gods had to fight against (and possibly demonize) to justify their own position.<br /> <br /> Medusa's fate was so unjust.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard that the Titans actually sparked a golden age for humanity during their rule. Not sure how accurate that may actually be, I would have to look it up to confirm it. The Greek gods were incredibly selfish and arrogant. Turning a woman into a spider just because she can spin thread better than you is a bit of an extreme reaction, don't you think? And yeah, cursing Medusa with extreme hideousness because she was raped by the god of the sea is equally unnerving.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, people seem to be missing the &gt;:3 face I made under my earlier comment, indicating I was trying to make a joke. Didn't mean to offend anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-02-2013, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:02:37-08:00","id":21733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=21724#post21724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I heard that the Titans actually sparked a golden age for humanity during their rule. Not sure how accurate that may actually be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your definition of Golden Age. Hediod and Plato both describe the Golden Age as being Golden because Kronos set the Daimones to oversee man and make all decisions for them. By their accounts it wasn't so much a time when man broke no rules as it was a time when man had no idea that rules could be broken. Complete Peace, at the cost of Zero Freedom. When Zeus removed the Daimones, he gave us free will, and all the dangers that come with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:05:44-08:00","id":21738,"title":"","content":"Greeks confuse the issue grandly because not only do we get the concept (and word) of &quot;titans&quot; from them, but the titans themselves are nothing but the 2nd generation divine beings anyway. The originals are so vastly powerful and alien that they have never really been challenged or characterized. You never hear of Nyx (Night) or Chronos (Time, <i>different from Kronos!</i>) acting up the way the 2nd and 3rd gen deities did, and Oceanus (the original Ocean being) is never mentioned other than simply being there and spawning tons of daughters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:10:24-08:00","id":21742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=21724#post21724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard that the Titans actually sparked a golden age for humanity during their rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>The benefits of the golden age are rather nebulous. There was plenty to eat, good health, and effective immortality. But neither was there progress, innovation, or freedom. So, all of the pros of being a happy immortal cow and all of the cons of being a happy immortal cow. I guess it is up to the individual to decide if all this neat stuff like the internet and houses were worth it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, people seem to be missing the &gt;:3 face I made under my earlier comment, indicating I was trying to make a joke. Didn't mean to offend anyone. </div> </div> </div>Probably a colloquialism. It looks like an angry cat to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:15:52-08:00","id":21747,"title":"","content":"I think Prometheus could use a little love.<br /> <br /> Wow, the website went from ok to sucksville. Took me half an hour to post anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:47:00-08:00","id":21764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=21668#post21668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo there will be a setting for Scion 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Four settings, with the option of more, <a href=\"http://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comments/17mu3l/we_are_onyx_pathwhite_wolf_amaask_us_anything/c872ayc\" target=\"_blank\">from what Joe's said</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:39:06-08:00","id":22417,"title":"","content":"I presume, that is good place to ask some questions that I have not ask at the old forum.<br /> 1) How are Favored Abilities denoted? I mean, we have rules for Associated Purviews and Epic Attributes - whatever debatable they are - but I cannot remember anything about Abilities. At first I thought that the highest are taken, but... Well, for example, Set has Brawl, Command, Control, Melee, Presence and Survival as inherited. And his writeup lists four of them at 5 - along with Athletics, Awareness, Fortitude and Integrity. Actually, Control and Presence are 4 - but they are inherited, while others are not.<br /> The same is with Hera. She has Fortitude of 4, others Favored at 5 - and has also Art, Awareness and Integrity at 5, for example.<br /> So - how?<br /> <br /> 2) It is well-known that characters are upgraded, when they become Demigods, receiving certain number of points on Attributes, for example. And at least 2 of these points should go into category. And we know that no mundane Attribute cannot exceed Legend.<br /> So. If I have a character with Legend 4 and, for example, Strength 5, Dexterity 5 and Stamina 4... what should I do with Demigod upgrade at Legend 5? Even if I list Physical Attributes as tertiary, I should place 2 points at this category, so I can raise Stamina to 5... and what with the other point?<br /> I can imagine two variants of solving this problem, but, perhaps, someone already solved it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I must - so I can.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Learning makes life more rewarding and enjoyable;...the worst thing of all is ignorance</span>.</i> <div align=\"right\">Alfred the Great</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1425-vi-zet","name":"Vi-Zet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T15:15:20-08:00","id":22628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=22417#post22417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume, that is good place to ask some questions that I have not ask at the old forum.<br /> 1) How are Favored Abilities denoted? I mean, we have rules for Associated Purviews and Epic Attributes - whatever debatable they are - but I cannot remember anything about Abilities. At first I thought that the highest are taken, but... Well, for example, Set has Brawl, Command, Control, Melee, Presence and Survival as inherited. And his writeup lists four of them at 5 - along with Athletics, Awareness, Fortitude and Integrity. Actually, Control and Presence are 4 - but they are inherited, while others are not.<br /> The same is with Hera. She has Fortitude of 4, others Favored at 5 - and has also Art, Awareness and Integrity at 5, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion RAW picked abilities and Associateds which the developers thought fit the God in question for passing down to their children, and the writers of the Scion Godbook weren't aware of any rule that those abilities should be all 5 or whatnot. <i>Then again</i> the mechanical sheets of any stated character in the RAW books was kinda horrifying in their lack of anything resembling balance or sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=22417#post22417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) It is well-known that characters are upgraded, when they become Demigods, receiving certain number of points on Attributes, for example. And at least 2 of these points should go into category. And we know that no mundane Attribute cannot exceed Legend.<br /> So. If I have a character with Legend 4 and, for example, Strength 5, Dexterity 5 and Stamina 4... what should I do with Demigod upgrade at Legend 5? Even if I list Physical Attributes as tertiary, I should place 2 points at this category, so I can raise Stamina to 5... and what with the other point?<br /> I can imagine two variants of solving this problem, but, perhaps, someone already solved it?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW-wise? No. You've essentially lost a dot of attribute. An ST could let you move that extra dot to another category, or one could remove the idea of categories all together and just give flat-across-the-board increases. (9 total instead of 4/3/2). What my groups do is allow Demigods to have Attributes rated to 8, and Gods to 11. This completely removes the conflict and allows characters to have some diversity when they hit the respective legend-bumps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T19:33:51-08:00","id":22827,"title":"","content":"So anybody know why The Scion Wiki got taken down and replaced with this...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.white-wolf.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> For the past few days I was getting a lot of information off the wiki, now every time I click on a link, it takes me to White-wolf.com, and doesn't have any place to research the game side from buying the books on Drivthru.<br /> <br /> D:&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T19:42:06-08:00","id":22831,"title":"","content":"White Wolf restructured its web-properties. Poops, that means all my work on cataloguing Necromancy is gone, too. Darn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T00:54:20-08:00","id":23002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=22628#post22628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scion RAW picked abilities and Associateds which the developers thought fit the God in question for passing down to their children, and the writers of the Scion Godbook weren't aware of any rule that those abilities should be all 5 or whatnot. <i>Then again</i> the mechanical sheets of any stated character in the RAW books was kinda horrifying in their lack of anything resembling balance or sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Thank you for answer.<br /> Personally I would say that in case of Abilities every God chooses for him/herself, and the only restriction - 4 or 5 level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RAW-wise? No. You've essentially lost a dot of attribute. An ST could let you move that extra dot to another category, or one could remove the idea of categories all together and just give flat-across-the-board increases. (9 total instead of 4/3/2). What my groups do is allow Demigods to have Attributes rated to 8, and Gods to 11. This completely removes the conflict and allows characters to have some diversity when they hit the respective legend-bumps. </div> </div> </div>Ah. Interesting, I should take it into account. I personally thought about two other possibilities:<br /> 1) convert this dot into 4 bonus points;<br /> 2) &quot;save it&quot;, and let the character to have one experience-free Attribute increase the next time Legend goes up.<br /> Thanks for answer again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I must - so I can.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Learning makes life more rewarding and enjoyable;...the worst thing of all is ignorance</span>.</i> <div align=\"right\">Alfred the Great</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1425-vi-zet","name":"Vi-Zet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:36:27-08:00","id":25520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=22827#post22827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So anybody know why The Scion Wiki got taken down and replaced with this...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.white-wolf.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> For the past few days I was getting a lot of information off the wiki, now every time I click on a link, it takes me to White-wolf.com, and doesn't have any place to research the game side from buying the books on Drivthru.<br /> <br /> D:&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it kind of sucks as I was looking for the game errata for a new game I am about to start. Anybody have a link to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:41:10-08:00","id":25590,"title":"","content":"The very same announcement which declared that the WW forums would be closing to be replaced by the OPP forums also said that the WW Wikis would be shutting down.<br /> <br /> There's a thread about it here. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/22834-onyx-path-and-the-white-wolf-wiki\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...hite-wolf-wiki</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:00:46-08:00","id":25703,"title":"","content":"General question by new guy trying to run a game, Legend points are calculated by legend rating squared, so legend of 2 is 4 points legend 4 16?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:18:13-08:00","id":25711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=25703#post25703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General question by new guy trying to run a game, Legend points are calculated by legend rating squared, so legend of 2 is 4 points legend 4 16?</div> </div> </div> </div>Legend 2 = 4<br /> Legend 3 = 9<br /> Legend 4 = 16<br /> Legend 5 = 25<br /> Legend 6 = 36<br /> Legend 7 = 49<br /> Legend 8 = 64<br /> Legend 9 = 81<br /> Legend 10 = 100<br /> Legend 11 = 121<br /> Legend 12 = 144<br /> <br /> I've been running this game for at least three years and I still have to double-check every time someone goes up in Legend or I'm making a new NPC/PC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:33:41-08:00","id":25722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=25711#post25711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Legend 2 = 4<br /> Legend 3 = 9<br /> Legend 4 = 16<br /> Legend 5 = 25<br /> Legend 6 = 36<br /> Legend 7 = 49<br /> Legend 8 = 64<br /> Legend 9 = 81<br /> Legend 10 = 100<br /> Legend 11 = 121<br /> Legend 12 = 144<br /> <br /> I've been running this game for at least three years and I still have to double-check every time someone goes up in Legend or I'm making a new NPC/PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! My group roped me into Dming, and I love the concept so its campaign design and book comb overs for the next few weeks XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T06:42:12-08:00","id":26469,"title":"","content":"With the &quot;Epic Appearance&quot; stat, does that only apply to the particular God's &quot;flavor&quot; of Epic Appearance? IE, are Scions of Izanami always exceptionally repulsive with their Epic Appearance or can they be the opposite?<br /> <br /> If the former, is Kali's Epic Appearance the gorgeous kind or the not-so-good looking kind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T07:06:46-08:00","id":26480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=26469#post26469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &quot;Epic Appearance&quot; stat, does that only apply to the particular God's &quot;flavor&quot; of Epic Appearance? IE, are Scions of Izanami always exceptionally repulsive with their Epic Appearance or can they be the opposite?<br /> <br /> If the former, is Kali's Epic Appearance the gorgeous kind or the not-so-good looking kind?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>That is entirely the decision of your storyteller. </b>The books themselves offer no conclusive answers about Epic Appearance or Animal. <br /> <br /> A strict interpretation means if your parent says Epic Appearance (Negative) and Animal (Bee) then you can ONLY get a discount if you buy Epic Appearance (Negative) and Animal (Bee).<br /> <br /> A loose interpretation means if your parent says Epic Appearance (Negative) and Animal (Bee) then you can still get a discount if you buy Epic Appearance (Positive) and Animal (Bull).<br /> <br /> Some storytellers fall in the middle and let you pick up animals in the same general Family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:26:17-08:00","id":26694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=26480#post26480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some storytellers fall in the middle and let you pick up animals in the same general Family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run things with Animal always applying to a Family, by the scientific defintion. This prevents the problem the books have with some deities having animal for broad groups and some for very specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T23:03:38-08:00","id":27018,"title":"","content":"Another question I have is in regards to the realms and the titans. I've been spending the last several days constructing a fan made Pantheon with 14 Primary Gods (as in those who are not Scions), but in order to complete the information, I need to come up with an idea for an Underworld, and Overworld, and an Arch Titan for them to be enemies with. How exactly do these realms and titans work?<br /> <br /> <br /> The 4 virtues for the Pantheon are Expression, Loyalty, Harmony, and Endurance, so I was thinking that a Titan who embodies selfishness, chaos, weakness, and submission would be appropriate, but I don't know if that's how they work or not. All I know about the Titans is they apparently embody aspects of reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> What is needed for the construction of a proper Over / Underworld, and how do Arch Titans work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T00:10:10-08:00","id":27039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=27018#post27018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question I have is in regards to the realms and the titans. I've been spending the last several days constructing a fan made Pantheon with 14 Primary Gods (as in those who are not Scions), but in order to complete the information, I need to come up with an idea for an Underworld, and Overworld, and an Arch Titan for them to be enemies with. How exactly do these realms and titans work?<br /> <br /> <br /> The 4 virtues for the Pantheon are Expression, Loyalty, Harmony, and Endurance, so I was thinking that a Titan who embodies selfishness, chaos, weakness, and submission would be appropriate, but I don't know if that's how they work or not. All I know about the Titans is they apparently embody aspects of reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> What is needed for the construction of a proper Over / Underworld, and how do Arch Titans work?</div> </div> </div> </div>The books aren't super specific on that front, so I'd look at the ones they've already set up, and see if you can work from one of those. If you can tell us anything more about what you're building, I know I, and probably ohters on the forums, would be happy to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T06:46:02-08:00","id":27156,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to look for just that, but since the wiki I had been using was now taken down, it's become a lot harder to find information regarding the current existing pantheons.<br /> <br /> <br /> The fan pantheon that I created has some resemblance to shamanism, involving animal spirit guides instead of human based deities. It's also from the modern age, the gods being depicts of a new age culture and drawing strength from their beliefs and customs. Which is why I was looking for assistance in how to create the necessary roles I was looking for, I didn't know how an Arch Titan would be chosen for a newly arisen Pantheon, since they're supposed to be ancient beings.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been able to learn that the Overworlds and Underworlds are all on the same plane as each other, but the gods just 'divide' territories for their pantheons to rule. So essentially they'd be next door neighbors with the Pesedjet, or the Dodekatheon. However, I wasn't able to figure out how the construction of such realms works.<br /> <br /> Do they just find an empty plot of dimensional space and start building it?<br /> <br /> <br /> I also needed to know if the Underworlds are similar to Hades where Hell, Heaven, and Limbo are all located in the same place. If that's the case, I may need to create multiple versions of the Underworld to suit the fates of their worshipers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-10-2013, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:45:15-08:00","id":27187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=27156#post27156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been trying to look for just that, but since the wiki I had been using was now taken down, it's become a lot harder to find information regarding the current existing pantheons.<br /> <br /> The fan pantheon that I created has some resemblance to shamanism, involving animal spirit guides instead of human based deities. It's also from the modern age, instead of ancient times, which is why I was looking for assistance in how to create the necessary roles I was looking for, I didn't know how an Arch Titan would be chosen for a newly arisen Pantheon, since they're supposed to be ancient beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. In that case, I think it'd be more about which Titan's attention you draw - basically, which avatar of a Titan your pantheon offends enough (or vice versa) to gain a special place on their hit-list. They may be ancient, but you _really_ piss them off.<br /> <br /> Titans generally represent single, broad-ranging concepts, such as Fire, Water, Love, Time, Justice, Chaos, etc. It's not necessarily that you hold opposing Virtues, but that you represent a concept at odds with theirs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been able to learn that the Overworlds and Underworlds are all on the same plane as each other, but the gods just 'divide' territories for their pantheons to rule. So essentially they'd be next door neighbors with the Pesedjet, or the Dodekatheon. However, I wasn't able to figure out how the construction of such realms works.<br /> <br /> Do they just find an empty plot of dimensional space and start building it? </div> </div> </div>A new pantheon can build their own Godrealm, or move into a pre-existing empty one. They're not bound by the rules of mortal space-time: want eternal summer or winter? No problem. Want to have a Godrealm as large as a palace contain subrealms as large as Earth? Again, no problem. The Overworld is infinite, and contains infinities - the Godrealms and Titan-Realms. Being infinite, the Overworld is large enough that Godrealms don't overlap.<br /> <br /> One thing their Godrealm will have, however, is an Axis Mundi, a location that allows them to travel between their Godrealm and the mortal World. It'll be a location strongly associated with their pantheon (as Yggdrasil, the World Tree, is strongly associated with the Aesir).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also needed to know if the Underworlds are similar to Hades where Hell, Heaven, and Limbo are all located in the same place. If that's the case, I may need to create multiple versions of the Underworld to suit the fates of their worshipers. </div> </div> </div>Kind of. Not all pantheons see the Underworld like that - the Amatsukami and the Loa, for example, don't judge their dead believers, and welcome them all into their respective Underworlds. Other pantheons divide up their Underworlds into places of punishment and reward. Some have their Underworld as a trial prior to reincarnation.<br /> <br /> Underworlds, too, have links to the mortal World - times, places, and practices strongly associated with death for that pantheon, via which a Scion can venture into the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:58:23-08:00","id":27193,"title":"","content":"Alright, thank you! I managed to find a website that explains a bit about the pre-existing Titans. After looking through them, I believe that Hundun, the Greater Titan of Chaos would be appropriately suitable. According to what I read on him, he likes to corrupt others gods into doing his bidding, as opposed to creating his own Titan avatars.<br /> <br /> <br /> With this information, I should be able to complete the details I needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T08:42:44-08:00","id":27212,"title":"","content":"Do Scions need to manifest aspects of Epic Attributes before their Visitation or is it perfectly acceptable for say a petite bookworm who can barely manage a push-up to lifting 500 pounds with the first dot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:54:14-08:00","id":27270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=27212#post27212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Scions need to manifest aspects of Epic Attributes before their Visitation or is it perfectly acceptable for say a petite bookworm who can barely manage a push-up to lifting 500 pounds with the first dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Scions might be exceptional mortals before they're Visited, but they're simply mortal. No epics. So that meek bookworm is going to be surprised when after Daddy Ares' visit, she finds that she can pick up the shelf, let along the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T15:12:30-08:00","id":28328,"title":"","content":"Soak...<br /> &quot;Bashing: STA, + special from Epic&quot;<br /> &quot;Lethal: if Scion = Bash/2 + special from Epic&quot;<br /> &quot;Agg: Special from Epic&quot;<br /> <br /> Soooo...<br /> Sta: 3 + 2 Epic =<br /> B: 5 (3 STA + epic)<br /> L: 5 (5B/2 + 2 Epic)<br /> A: 2 (Epic)<br /> <br /> Or is lethal actually 4 (STA/2 + epic)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:22:04-08:00","id":28409,"title":"","content":"Okay, clarification on soak...<br /> <br /> Let's say you have a guy with 4 Stamina and 3 Epic Stamina.<br /> <br /> Bashing is Stamina + the autosuccesses from Epic Stamina. So the Bashing Soak would be 8 (4+4)<br /> <br /> Lethal is Stamina/2 + Epic Stamina autosuccesses. So, Lethal soak would be 6 (2+4)<br /> <br /> Aggravated soak is equal to the dots of Epic Stamina. So, Aggravated soak would be 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T20:40:15-08:00","id":28501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=28409#post28409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, clarification on soak...<br /> Lethal is Stamina/2 + Epic Stamina autosuccesses. So, Lethal soak would be 6 (2+4)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the RAW says that Lethal is *Bash*/2 not Stamina/2...<br /> <br /> Hopefully Scion 2e will fix these types of &quot;Well, we said this, but meant that...just use comon sense, instead of RAW.&quot; issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T21:12:56-08:00","id":28521,"title":"","content":"Scion 1e had this tendency to not factor Epic Attributes into anything, or at least underestimate their importance. It's quite weird at times. They probably meant that calculation to be before Epic Stamina was applied...<br /> <br /> It should be noted that all the listed Lethal Soak values involved halving Stamina before applying Epics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T10:54:10-08:00","id":28814,"title":"","content":"By the way, how does death function in the world of Scion? If a soul is killed in the underworld, does it just reform at a later time, or does it cease to exist; and does death work differently for mortals and Deities?<br /> <br /> One review I watched on youtube claimed that it's possible for players to journey to the Underworld and rescue their allies from death, so I'm guessing it's a little more than simply &quot;you're dead, game over!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:23:29-08:00","id":28929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=28814#post28814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, how does death function in the world of Scion? If a soul is killed in the underworld, does it just reform at a later time, or does it cease to exist; and does death work differently for mortals and Deities?<br /> <br /> One review I watched on youtube claimed that it's possible for players to journey to the Underworld and rescue their allies from death, so I'm guessing it's a little more than simply &quot;you're dead, game over!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is up to the ST, some might kill them, but I think most just send them to the Underworld to be recycled as antagonists and use them again and again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T23:05:45-08:00","id":29171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=28929#post28929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is up to the ST, some might kill them, but I think most just send them to the Underworld to be recycled as antagonists and use them again and again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to be noticing a lot of people saying that ST's have the freedom to diverge from the rule books in Whitewolf games. It seems they're only meant to be used as guide lines, not iron clad systems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T23:43:37-08:00","id":29177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=29171#post29171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to be noticing a lot of people saying that ST's have the freedom to diverge from the rule books in Whitewolf games. It seems they're only meant to be used as guide lines, not iron clad systems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The 1st edition of Scion required so many houserules that we have built up a culture based around accepting the fact that almost nobody is playing exactly the same game. Some forums look down upon houserules, but here it is just an accepted part of life <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T01:25:44-08:00","id":29200,"title":"","content":"Im looking for the Vedic and yankee pantheons, I know the persian is in the yazata, are the others as well? I think i can get it on drive through but the others may be necessary in the budding game, does anyone know where they are located?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T07:17:44-08:00","id":29288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=29200#post29200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im looking for the Vedic and yankee pantheons, I know the persian is in the yazata, are the others as well? I think i can get it on drive through but the others may be necessary in the budding game, does anyone know where they are located?</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest thing you will find to the old Vedic pantheon are The Deva located in Companion, Part 5. Generally you will have better luck with <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/deva.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The Deva</a>, which is more heavily researched than what you will find in the Companion.<br /> <br /> The mostly fictional Yankee pantheon can be found in Companion, Part 6. Telgar might be able to show you his recreation of the Yankees, but I do not know if that effort was eaten by the old forums or if he saved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T01:13:21-08:00","id":29804,"title":"","content":"Thank you! My next questiion is less scion more general wod i suppose, looking at the battlewheel it looks like everyone rolls their initiative, are placed on their assorted ticks and then take their turns? for instance, if your taking a action on tick 0 and your action takes three ticks to happen it does not resolve until tick 3? in which case your now on click three? and you must wait the speed before taking another action?<br /> <br /> EX: Joe takes an action on click 1 and Bill takes an action on click 1 joe aims that is a 3 click action, does he move 3 clicks up and wait until the tick counter reaches click 4 before his action resolves, meanwhile Bill flees, they happen at the same time so Bill moves his dex in yards for these three clicks?<br /> <br /> Now, assuming that is correct, while Joe is aiming he has a -1 to Defense value? Until click 4 when the action resolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T01:19:43-08:00","id":29805,"title":"","content":"Your action resolves on the tick you start with, then you're waiting until your next tick before taking another action. If you attack someone with a Speed 4 action on Tick 1, then your attack is resolved on Tick 1. After 4 ticks pass (Tick 5 now), you get another action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T01:32:32-08:00","id":29807,"title":"","content":"Ahh okay, so with something like coordinated attack if you coordinate on tick 1 people need to be able to act on tick 6 this means they can take any action that doesnt put them waiting past tick 6? Because they need to all act on that tick even if their ticks passed?<br /> <br /> Joe coordinates attack on bill with Mark kim and john<br /> <br /> mark and kim act on tick 2<br /> john acts on tick 3<br /> <br /> they can take actions respectively at 4 and 3 speed without ruining the coordinated attack? Or could they just wait and guard until tick 6?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T02:44:57-08:00","id":29815,"title":"","content":"Yes, someone intending to participate in a Coordinated Attack on Tick 6 can do whatever they want until then, so long as they are able to act on Tick 6. If they take a Speed 5 action on Tick 4, they will not be able to act on Tick 6 and will get left out of the Coordinated Attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T09:35:27-08:00","id":29958,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, all right a question on attacking, the base difficulty thing, is that like a set number somewhere or variable? An attack against base difficulty-D means what exactly, where is the difficulty coming from if the players defensive value is the penalty from attacking him already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T11:53:51-08:00","id":30020,"title":"","content":"The base difficulty in Scion is always 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T13:01:20-08:00","id":30066,"title":"","content":"Awesome, now a question with epic stamina,and forgive the endless questions O_O but if you have 2 points in epic stamina you ignore wound penalties until you get to -4? the one before incapacitated, and if you have epic stamina 3 you just dont have wound penalties?<br /> <br /> also, im torn the groups using this mmp sight to build characters which pulls from all the books, are the boons knacks and so forth in demigod demigod only? Can they get a 4 dot boon or a knack that needs a prereq? Is this a ST thing or is there rules somewhere for this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1584,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","user":"Oberon","date":". 12-14-2013, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T14:14:01-08:00","id":30096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30066#post30066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, now a question with epic stamina,and forgive the endless questions O_O but if you have 2 points in epic stamina you ignore wound penalties until you get to -4? the one before incapacitated, and if you have epic stamina 3 you just dont have wound penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, both are correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30066#post30066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, im torn the groups using this mmp sight to build characters which pulls from all the books, are the boons knacks and so forth in demigod demigod only? Can they get a 4 dot boon or a knack that needs a prereq? Is this a ST thing or is there rules somewhere for this</div> </div> </div> </div>You can buy Boons ranked below your Legend, e.i. to buy a 4 dot Boon you need to be at Legend 5 (thus possibly being a Demigod, but the upgrade to demigod can be retarded by the ST to allow a group to advance to Demigodhood together).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T14:23:16-08:00","id":30098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30066#post30066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, now a question with epic stamina,and forgive the endless questions O_O but if you have 2 points in epic stamina you ignore wound penalties until you get to -4? the one before incapacitated, and if you have epic stamina 3 you just dont have wound penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Epic Stamina 1 reduces the wound penalties to -0, -1, and -3 respectively. Epic Stamina 2 reduces the wound penalties to -0, -0, and -2 respectively. Epic Stamina 3 reduces the wound penalties to -0, -0, and -0 respectively. This also means injuries heal faster because you treat them as -0 health boxes. And yes, this means if you have Epic Stamina 3 you no longer suffer wound penalties. You might still experience pain, of course, but that becomes a personal choice up to the individual character.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30066#post30066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, im torn the groups using this mmp sight to build characters which pulls from all the books, are the boons knacks and so forth in demigod demigod only? Can they get a 4 dot boon or a knack that needs a prereq? Is this a ST thing or is there rules somewhere for this</div> </div> </div> </div>Knacks from any source can be used by any Tier of character as long as you have all prerequisite knacks (except Sense Prayers). A Hero could have Anti-Gravity Climber provided that he first purchased Spider Climber and Monkey Climber.<br /> <br /> You can only buy boons at a level equal to Permanent Legend -1. You do not need to have a relic that channels that purview to buy them, though it is necessary to actually use that boon as a Hero. You can choose to put Boons on your Relics instead, but Heroes cannot have Boons worth more than 3 dots at character creation. For example, a Legend 2 Hero could not buy Unquiet Corpse because she can only buy Legend 1 Boons, but she could spend 3 dots on a Relic that grants her Unquiet Corpse. But she could not spend 4 dots on a Relic that grants her Summon Ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T14:43:02-08:00","id":30104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30098#post30098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epic Stamina 1 reduces the wound penalties to -0, -1, and -3 respectively. Epic Stamina 2 reduces the wound penalties to -0, -0, and -2 respectively. Epic Stamina 3 reduces the wound penalties to -0, -0, and -0 respectively. This also means injuries heal faster because you treat them as -0 health boxes. And yes, this means if you have Epic Stamina 3 you no longer suffer wound penalties. You might still experience pain, of course, but that becomes a personal choice up to the individual character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to say that the way I read it is that the first dot of Epic Stamina turns -1 penalties to -0 penalties, the second turns -2 penalties to -0 penalties and the third turns -4 penalties to -0 penalties. I believe that this is the correct reading, because it is coherent with the way the characters are presented in Demigod (See Donnie in page 43 on Scion: Demigod).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30098#post30098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knacks from any source can be used by any Tier of character as long as you have all prerequisite knacks (except Sense Prayers). A Hero could have Anti-Gravity Climber provided that he first purchased Spider Climber and Monkey Climber.<br /> <br /> You can only buy boons at a level equal to Permanent Legend -1. You do not need to have a relic that channels that purview to buy them, though it is necessary to actually use that boon as a Hero. You can choose to put Boons on your Relics instead, but Heroes cannot have Boons worth more than 3 dots at character creation. For example, a Legend 2 Hero could not buy Unquiet Corpse because she can only buy Legend 1 Boons, but she could spend 3 dots on a Relic that grants her Unquiet Corpse. But she could not spend 4 dots on a Relic that grants her Summon Ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>But all of this is absolutely correct. Sorry about forgetting about the Knacks, had a phone call and decided to just post it like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T14:53:41-08:00","id":30107,"title":"","content":"Pantheon specific purviews at creation, with the 10 dots of boons and knacks, is that one for one or do you have to get those with bonus xp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:00:04-08:00","id":30109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oberon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30107#post30107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pantheon specific purviews at creation, with the 10 dots of boons and knacks, is that one for one or do you have to get those with bonus xp?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pantheon Specific Purviews are bought in the same way as Special Purviews, you increase their rating linearly. That is if you have 2 dots in a PSP you have the first and the second Boons; and you only need to buy the third dot to get the third Boon. So you can allocate 3 dots of Boons and Epics to a PSP and get 3 different Boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T18:27:21-08:00","id":30187,"title":"","content":"So you get a free Knack when you get a dot of an Epic Attribute, right? Does that apply at chargen?<br /> <br /> So for example I'll just use the petite bookworm from before. On character gen, they get two dots of Epic Strength. Would they get any of the two knacks presented for free or at chargen does the dots from the Boon/Knack pool have to be spent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T22:14:45-08:00","id":30273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=30187#post30187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you get a free Knack when you get a dot of an Epic Attribute, right? Does that apply at chargen?<br /> <br /> So for example I'll just use the petite bookworm from before. On character gen, they get two dots of Epic Strength. Would they get any of the two knacks presented for free or at chargen does the dots from the Boon/Knack pool have to be spent?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T07:23:28-07:00","id":702056,"title":"","content":"Wow, I've been gone forever and am only just now getting back into playing Scion... *and* [im]patiently waiting for 2.0...<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, found the rules.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Meanwhile, I have a Query about the durations of strenuous activities when one has Epic Stamina.<br /> <br /> Holding your breath is clearly defined. Starving is clearly defined. Dehydration is clearly defined... Fatigue from strenuous activities is only *clearly* defined when you have no Epic Stamina.<br /> (STA + Fortitude) / 2 Hours. The RAW mention that Epic Stamina affects this, but nowhere that I've found does it specify exactly *HOW* it modifies the number.<br /> <br /> To add to (or compound) the problem, both Holy Fortitude (from Hero) and Divine Fortitude (from Demigod) &quot;double&quot; the previous. Very poor wording Divine Fortitude [incorrectly?} implies that the Epic Stamina bonus effects the base duration, and then the initial doubled duration, which is then doubled again for Divine.<br /> <br /> Assuming Stamina 4, Epic Stamina 2, Fortitude 1, and both the above knacks.<br /> <br /> ( ( 4 + 1 + 2) / 2 [base] ) * 4 [both knacks] = 16 hrs.<br /> <br /> <b>( ( ( 4 + 1 ) / 2 [base] ) + 2 [Epic] ) * 4 [both knacks] = 20 hrs.</b><br /> <br /> ( ( ( ( ( 4 + 1 ) / 2 [base] ) + 2 [Epic] ) * 2 [Holy Fort] ) + 2 [Epic again, because Divine Fort] ) * 2 [Divine Fort] = 24 hrs.<br /> <br /> *<b>bold</b>* is my default guess.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","user":"sprunka","date":".  Found the rules. 10-15-2015, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}